{
  "summary": "Call with Maya (them), with Yossi (operations) joining on shipping questions. The client is a chain of 14 container stores that wants online ordering with delivery time windows; today orders come by phone and a shared spreadsheet. The launch target is before the holidays, and they must go live within four weeks. Management approved a budget of about 45,000 ש\"ח for the whole project. The catalog has about 4,000 SKUs, with roughly a third (about 1,300) online at launch. Open questions: whether we can connect to their inventory system (an old system on a local server, its vendor closed; Yossi will send the manual by email today); how delivery windows should work (two-hour windows, with a per-store cap per window); whether we handle storage and maintenance after launch (we have a package, to be detailed in the proposal); whether Ilan, the decision maker, can join the next call; and whether we handle pickup lockers in stores. Maya received a competing quote from a larger firm at about half our price and is worried about it; we agreed to compare it line by line. Payments go through a payment provider, so card details never touch their server. A loyalty app was raised and deferred. Yossi will send the delivery zone file after the call. Dan promised a sample proposal.",
  "resolve": [],
  "update": [
    {"id": "q3", "fields": {"text": "me to them: אילן יוכל להצטרף לשיחה הבאה? (תשובה: אולי)"}}
  ]
}
